              "description": "Display label of the inverse relation field created on the target object",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "targetObjectMetadataId": {
              "description": "Target object ID",
              "format": "uuid",
              "type": "string",
            },
            "type": {
              "description": "Relation direction from the perspective of the object the field is created on. MANY_TO_ONE: the field points to a single target record; this object owns the foreign key and gets a writable '<fieldName>Id' on its create/update inputs. Use it for 'belongs to one' fields. ONE_TO_MANY: the field is a read-only collection of target records; records are linked by writing the inverse '<fieldName>Id' on the target object.",
              "enum": [
                "MANY_TO_ONE",
                "ONE_TO_MANY",
