    "description": "Check a validation rule expression against an object without saving anything. An invalid expression is rejected with the reason.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "properties": {
        "expression": {
          "description": "Condition that must be true for a record to be saved. When it is false, the write is rejected and the message is shown. Reference fields by name, as returned by get_field_metadata. Use dot access for a composite field part (amount.amountMicros, name.firstName) and for a field of a many-to-one related record (company.name), never brackets. Compare select and multi-select fields with option values, e.g. stage == 'CUSTOMER'. Currency amounts are in micros: amount.amountMicros > 1000000000 means more than 1000. Write text in single quotes. Operators: == != < <= > >= + - * / and or not, and value in [a, b]. now is the date and time of the write; true and false are booleans. Functions: isDefined(value) is true when the value is set, even to an empty text; isEmpty(value) is true when the value is not set, an empty text, an empty list, or a composite field with every part empty; isNonEmptyString(value); includes(listOrText, value) is true when a multi-select or array contains the value, or a text contains a text, case-sensitive; arrayLength(list). To require a field, use not isEmpty(field).",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "objectName": {
          "description": "Object name, singular or plural (e.g. "company" or "companies").",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "objectName",
        "expression",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "validate_validation_rule_expression",
  },
  {
